.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \(dqbashclient.h\(dq

void bc_free(void *ptr);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Frees a memory buffer that was allocated and returned by the
\f[CR]libbashclient\f[R] API.
This function is equivalent to \f[CR]free(3)\f[R] but is provided for
API consistency and to ensure that memory allocated by the library is
freed by the same allocator.
.PP
This is particularly important on Windows/Cygwin where different DLLs
may use different C runtime heap instances.
Using \f[CR]bc_free\f[R] guarantees that the correct heap is used
regardless of how the library is linked.
.PP
It is safe to call \f[CR]bc_free\f[R] with a NULL argument; the function
returns immediately without action.
