.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
For \f[CR]bc_eval_result_t\f[R] structures, prefer
\f[CR]bc_eval_result_free(3)\f[R] which frees both
\f[CR]stdout_data\f[R] and \f[CR]stderr_data\f[R] in one call and sets
the pointers to NULL.
Use \f[CR]bc_free\f[R] directly only when you need to free individual
fields or other API\-returned buffers.
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]bc_error(3)\f[R] function returns a pointer to an internal
static buffer that must NOT be freed with \f[CR]bc_free\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
On platforms where the library and application share the same C runtime
heap (typical on Linux/Cygwin with static linking), \f[CR]bc_free\f[R]
and \f[CR]free(3)\f[R] are interchangeable.
However, using \f[CR]bc_free\f[R] is recommended for portability.
.IP \(bu 2
Like \f[CR]free(3)\f[R], calling \f[CR]bc_free\f[R] on a pointer that
was not returned by the library, or calling it twice on the same
pointer, results in undefined behavior.
